    "body": "Fixes #8216\n\n### What does this PR do?\n\n`parallel_compute_score_async` in `PrimeRewardManager` had no branch for dict results, so dict-returning reward functions (math_dapo, rlla, ...) hit `float(result[0])`, raised `KeyError: 0`, and `verify()`'s except-all fallback silently zeroed the whole batch.\n\nThis adds the same `isinstance(result, dict) -> result[\"score\"]` handling that `NaiveRewardManager` / `BatchRewardManager` / `DAPORewardManager` already have.\n\n### Tests\n\nNew `tests/workers/reward_manager/test_prime_on_cpu.py` (CPU-only):\n- dict result -> uses \"score\" key (failed before this fix)\n- float / tuple (prime_math style) results unchanged\n- failing task still scores 0.0\n\nFull `tests/workers/reward_manager/` suite: 22 passed.\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
